<iscomment>
    Back-In-Stock "Notify Me" block (app_waitlist). Markup only -- all behaviour
    is in the bundled client module static/default/js/waitlist.js, and every
    user-visible string is rendered here via Resource.msg and read from data-*
    attributes so the JS carries no hardcoded copy.

    Self-contained: recomputes its own show/hide flag from the product model, so
    it renders correctly wherever the add-to-cart component is included. The
    block starts hidden (d-none) unless the resolved variant is out of stock;
    the client module flips it against the add-to-cart row on variant change.

    Cache-safe: no CSRF token is embedded (the PDP is page-cacheable). The button
    fetches a fresh session-bound token from WaitList-Token at click time.
</iscomment>
<iscomment>
    Same rule as the add-to-cart override: a resolved OOS variant, OR a fully
    sold-out variation master (productType master + aggregate !available), so a
    wholly out-of-stock style still offers Notify Me. Keyed to product.id (the
    master id in the fallback case).
</iscomment>
<isset name="wlNotifyShow" value="${!product.available && product.productType !== 'set' && product.productType !== 'bundle' && (product.readyToOrder || product.productType === 'master')}" scope="page" />

<div class="row waitlist-notify${wlNotifyShow ? '' : ' d-none'}" data-waitlist-block
    data-sku="${product.id}"
    data-token-url="${URLUtils.url('WaitList-Token')}"
    data-subscribe-url="${URLUtils.url('WaitList-Subscribe')}"
    data-before-login-url="${URLUtils.url('WaitList-BeforeLogin')}"
    data-login-url="${URLUtils.url('Login-Show')}"
    data-msg-cta="${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.cta', 'waitlist', null)}"
    data-msg-onlist="${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.onlist', 'waitlist', null)}"
    data-msg-already="${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.already', 'waitlist', null)}"
    data-msg-done="${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.done', 'waitlist', null)}"
    data-msg-alreadymsg="${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.alreadymsg', 'waitlist', null)}"
    data-msg-error="${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.error', 'waitlist', null)}"
    data-msg-neterror="${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.neterror', 'waitlist', null)}">
    <div class="col-12">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-block js-waitlist-notify">
            ${Resource.msg('waitlist.notify.cta', 'waitlist', null)}
        </button>
        <div class="waitlist-notify-msg" aria-live="polite"></div>
    </div>
</div>
